{
  "description": "Shared conformance cases for the filter spec (D-034). Every implementation (Python now: app/core/filter_spec.py; the browser in Phase 3) must select exactly `expected` (satcat_ids, in record order) for each valid case and reject each invalid one. Expected values are worked out by hand from the records below, not by running either implementation. Records are invented for the test, shaped like the objects dataset; a missing scalar is null, a missing list is null or []. Two placeholders keep the file short; runners expand them before use: clauses \"REPEAT_<n>\" means n copies of {\"field\": \"orbit_class\", \"op\": \"eq\", \"value\": \"LEO\"}, and a value \"LONG_<n>\" means a string of n letters A.",
